WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.330 --> 00:03.110
SodaComp is a soda company
based in Bonn, Germany.

2
00:03.560 --> 00:07.600
SodaComp's CEO has set an aggressive target:
to grow its European market share by 3%

3
00:07.600 --> 00:11.550
by the end of the year —
which is just five months away.

4
00:12.200 --> 00:15.620
A marketing team has been working away
on the problem for several weeks.

5
00:16.130 --> 00:20.320
First, they defined the problem
and have been using their problem question —

6
00:20.770 --> 00:25.250
“How can SodaComp improve its European
market share by 3% by the end of the year?”

7
00:25.610 --> 00:26.630
— to guide their thinking.

8
00:27.270 --> 00:30.800
The team drilled down on their problem question,
identified a number of issues,

9
00:30.800 --> 00:34.530
and hypothesised about
how they might be addressed.

10
00:35.140 --> 00:39.110
They prioritised two issues
and their associated hypotheses

11
00:39.490 --> 00:43.230
that they feel are central to addressing
the question of market share growth.

12
00:43.650 --> 00:46.910
Number one: to improve
their channel strategy.

13
00:47.270 --> 00:51.780
And number two: to innovate
with regard to product development.

14
00:52.610 --> 00:58.690
The team has shared this issue tree, and the research
and thinking that went into it, with SodaComp's CEO,

15
00:59.140 --> 01:03.600
who is pleased with their progress and is confident
the team has identified and prioritised

16
01:03.600 --> 01:08.640
the issues that are most important to consider,
and come up with strong hypotheses.

17
01:09.220 --> 01:12.200
The CEO has asked the team to move forward,

18
01:12.200 --> 01:15.010
and the team is now considering
what their next steps might be.
